WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.030 --> 00:00:03.950
We learn best when we're learning from
content that we find interesting.

00:00:03.950 --> 00:00:09.210
Comprehensible input or, as Stephen
Krashen, renowned expert on language...

00:00:09.210 --> 00:00:14.910
language acquisition calls it, compelling
content. So, make sure you choose material,

00:00:14.910 --> 00:00:19.920
choose lessons that interest you. You may
find them on your feed. These could be

00:00:19.920 --> 00:00:26.760
lessons that other people at LingQ are
studying. It could be newspaper articles

00:00:26.760 --> 00:00:32.790
that are regularly presented to you on
your feed. You may even want to import

00:00:32.790 --> 00:00:37.230
,and you should familiarize yourself with
the different ways of importing lessons.

00:00:37.230 --> 00:00:42.300
We have a... a Chrome extension and a
Google extension whereby you can... and

00:00:42.300 --> 00:00:47.190
also a Firefox extension, so that you can
import anything you find on the web. This

00:00:47.190 --> 00:00:52.590
is also available on your tablet. Make
sure you're familiar... you familiarize

00:00:52.590 --> 00:00:57.600
yourself. You can also import ebooks into
LingQ, and if you're smart, find the

00:00:57.600 --> 00:01:02.969
audiobook for it. So make sure you are
fully aware of how to bring interesting

00:01:02.969 --> 00:01:08.780
content into your learning space. It's
going to help your learning.

